{"requirements":[{"id":"centralized-log-delivery","requirement":"Forward node2 messages from the inventory application to node1 and persist them at /var/log/inventory/node2.log.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Rsyslog was configured on both nodes, node1 listened on TCP/514, and an inventory-tagged marker generated on node2 was directly observed in the required file on node1.","evidence_ids":["cmd-e9d902388b714915","cmd-bce8d711eae04616","cmd-28a33fcd1ce54bad","cmd-45625896ef0546ea","cmd-9c5bbdc1c1c74dea"]},{"id":"node1-restart-recovery","requirement":"Keep log collection and persistence working after node1 restarts.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The healthy pre-restart state was captured, reboot scheduling was acknowledged, node1's boot ID changed, rsyslog and the firewall listener recovered, existing log data remained, and a fresh node2 inventory message was received afterward.","evidence_ids":["cmd-fca4e661c3b34d03","cmd-5217958b0ce641da","cmd-3df6e28073f8402f","cmd-db1cb7c04dc8438c","cmd-6f9ec2290cea459e","cmd-582e9ba5d7054779","global:before_prepare:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity"]},{"id":"node2-restart-recovery","requirement":"Keep log forwarding working after node2 restarts.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The healthy pre-restart state was captured, reboot scheduling was acknowledged, node2's boot ID changed, enabled and active rsyslog recovered with a valid configuration, and a newly generated inventory message reached node1.","evidence_ids":["cmd-c9a56f13286d425f","cmd-51d2c5f35e0b44b9","cmd-ff3cecc56bb04b11","cmd-8e04ec82951e4dd8","cmd-712e8ac86a304045","global:before_prepare:node2:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node2:boot-identity"]},{"id":"platform-compatibility","requirement":"Retain the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with the platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Both nodes remained on AlmaLinux 9.6 with kernel 5.14.0-570.12.1.el9_6. The implementation used the already-installed AlmaLinux rsyslog 8.2412 package, and final package-health checks remained successful.","evidence_ids":["cmd-201139a44c23443c","cmd-f088582e88324cc1","global:before_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform","global:before_prepare:node2:platform","global:after_executor:node2:platform","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health"]}],"confidence":0.98,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified. Configuration-file creation, firewall changes, service restarts, bounded test messages, and both node reboots each directly supported implementation, final verification, or the mandatory restart protocol. No failed services, package damage, or abandoned temporary files were observed afterward; TCP/514 was the intentional collector endpoint.","evidence_ids":["cmd-e9d902388b714915","cmd-bce8d711eae04616","cmd-28a33fcd1ce54bad","cmd-4d074cb0b1d74d36","cmd-45625896ef0546ea","cmd-5217958b0ce641da","cmd-6f9ec2290cea459e","cmd-51d2c5f35e0b44b9","cmd-8e04ec82951e4dd8","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node2:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material outcomes are satisfied. Direct tests establish initial centralized delivery and successful recovery after separate restarts of node1 and node2. The provider-wide restart protocol is complete for both managed nodes and agrees with the fixed boot-identity observations. The operating-system release and kernel were retained, with no observed hygiene defects.","limitations":["Delivery was tested using inventory-tagged logger messages rather than captured output from a separately identified inventory application service; the evidence directly validates the configured routing path and message identity but not application-specific emission behavior beyond that interface."]}
